<<~ ahu slot=`#/b4-orchestration-collision-read-only-lines-are-o`>>

! b4-orchestration collision (Anvil-Four, 2026-10-31). Read-only; lines are open-node-vessel.ts unless noted.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/new-findings`>>

!! New findings (top)
N1. standSyncGates failed stand FAILS CLOSED inbound (ruling below). But three stale-revocation seams sit beside it:
a. STALE POSTURE ORDER (1274-1277): onRefold runs `dropNoLongerHeld()` (reads `postureOf` -> `gateReadings` cache, 1245) BEFORE `resweepGates()`, and gateReadings refreshes only inside `gateNexuses` (1487) during that later async sweep. A carried Nexus flipping open->private is judged on the OLD posture, so strangers' sockets stay seated (public shelf only) until the next refold; nothing re-runs the drop. Same cache serves the gate sorter (`posture: () => deps.posture(nexus)`), so a failed sweep keeps a stale-open posture for new knocks. Reach: public shelf, not private planes. Fails open-stale. Red: carried Nexus open, stranger seated, flip to private, fire onRefold, assert socket closed with no second refold.
b. NO SERIALIZATION (1514-1550): refold sweeps run concurrent and unqueued (`void resweepGates()`). The loop after `await gateNexuses()` is synchronous, but two sweeps can apply out of read order: an older set landing last re-stands a gate for an uncarried Nexus. Contrast intent-relay.ts:36-38 (`turn` chain, and read failure downs every gate = fail closed). The sync gates do the opposite on read failure: warn and keep the old set. Also `intentRelay === null` check races: two first sweeps can both call standIntentRelay (second hits "a gate already stands"). Unproven by test; narrowed to "possible".
c. The unstand loop (1519-1520) aborts the whole sweep on a throw, leaving later revoked gates standing. Low odds (unstand paths are idempotent), one-line red.
Per-dial admits read the held root fresh (vessel-gates.ts:44-46), so a stale standing gate does not admit a revoked presenter; the exposure is posture and socket lifetime.
N2. daemonAuth carries seeds for EVERY unlocked joined face (`joinedFaces` via joinedFaceAuth, 2511-2516), not only the worn atom (2532), plus hex address secret. A pure `buildDaemonAuth` returns secret-bearing data: red tests need sentinel seeds asserted absent from logs and JSON.stringify.
N3. Pool core hard-codes two more 10s deadlines (teardown ack 816, wiki place-verb 888) that T17 neither names nor injects.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/per-finding-rulings`>>

!! Per-finding rulings
* F1 herm wiki verbs TypeError: CONFIRMED. Registered at 3039-3231, bodies deref forward `let x!` (set only in makePool); composeNodeHermOn passes p.wireVerbs (3685). Fails closed (rejection on invoke; `wiki-act` is reachable by lares-cli shore-core.ts:157). Red: compose herm, assert the six verbs absent.
* F2: NARROWED. The 120s/3x PAIR has two literal homes (node 3386-3387 as 120_000/360_000; tw5 daemon-vm-core.ts:134,141, 3x derived). The pool default (10_000 via `??`, core 395-396) is a third, DIFFERENT value, not a third copy. `??` also passes 0/NaN through. No NodeVesselOptions knob exists. Wave 1's red/control stand.
* daemonAuth seed: CONFIRMED crossing, NOT a fault. island-protocol.ts:245-251 states wiki manifests omit it and the crossing is operator-confirmed custody. Island is a worker_thread, not a surface. Hygiene gap: `atomSeed` Uint8Array never zeroed (address secret is, 2080); hex copy is unzeroable.
* P6 gate-stand fail-mode (the open question): FAIL CLOSED inbound, rigorously: (1) only WS entry is `gateSync.wss` (766-770) fed solely through gateServer.handleUpgrade; no stood path -> http-face-dispatcher.ts:98-100 destroys the upgrade before 101; with no `opts.dispatcher` nothing routes at all. (2) Share verdict is independent: WS peer absent from peerIdentifierMap -> false (1021); class absent -> cross-operator. (3) Afterthe boot completes before gates stand (void, 3273): window is closed, not open. (4) resweepGates is assigned before the first stand (3272) so a later refold retries; with no refold, gates stay down (availability, not security). Residual: N1.

<<~/ahu>>

