<<~ ahu slot=`#/t14-vm-lift-research`>>

!! T14 VM-lift research (boot.js read in full, TiddlyWiki5/boot/boot.js:2553-2720)
* Ordering: tasks run in registration order unless `after`/`before` constrain. `after` naming a task that never runs (typo, wrong platform, disabled, or nameless module) leaves the dependent SILENTLY never run: the loop ends and the boot callback fires. So the witness must assert `$tw.lares.<x>Vm` is defined after boot, not just that the module is packed. A nameless module cannot be depended on.
* Sync default: `synchronous` absent = sync call (2632); a thenable return is awaited; a throw escapes execStartup and kills the island boot. Wrap startup bodies.
* House pattern: header `/*\ title/type: application/javascript/module-type: startup \*/`, `export const name`, pure `computeX`, `startup()` sets `$tw.lares.xVm` (worldline-read-vm.ts 149-163); query-derive-vm adds `after=["lararium-grammar-cache"]`. Pure subpath imports only (barrel drags wasm). plugin-build discover-modules walks src/ for headers, enforces unique title and output filename.
* Hidden coupling wave 1 missed: tests/goldens/filter-cts*.json list every startup module title; a new module regenerates those goldens. TW5 `platforms` knows only browser/node, so "daemon-only" cannot be module metadata; it rides plugin/offering selection (daemon resolves via resolveNodeIslandPluginCids recipe wikiSlug "daemon"), which T15 must witness.
* Module state is per VM (`let _causal`); no cross-island sharing.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/sources`>>

!! Sources (date-stamped 2026-10-31)
* TW5 boot.js, local, READ in full.
* https://tiddlywiki.com/dev/static/StartupMechanism.html (WebFetch; silent on missing-`after`, local source settles it).
* https://automerge.org/automerge-repo/interfaces/_automerge_automerge-repo.RepoConfig.html and ShareConfig types (SEARCH-ONLY): access vs announce split, default open; confirms house comment 1012-1016 that a bare sharePolicy leaves access open. The house verdict seats both hooks; house law stricter than default.
* https://wiki.owasp.org/index.php/Fail_securely (SEARCH-ONLY): exceptions in a control must not enable what it blocks; silent catch-alls flagged (matches `.catch(warn)`; fits inbound, not stale revocation). Revocation/stale-cache guidance not found.
* Conflict: outside practice says re-check/deny on read failure; house intent-relay does, sync gates keep the old set. No-global-now favors ordering by causal chain (serialize turns), not timers.

<<~/ahu>>

